INT. UNDERGROUND BOXING GYM - FORMER SUBWAY STATION - NIGHT

A tiled platform converted into a gym. A ring sits where the tracks used to run. Ceiling pipes sweat. Bare bulbs swing from wires. Old posters curl on the walls.

COACH IMELDA "MA" DUARTE-OSEI (60s, towel around neck, gnarled hands) wraps tape around a fighter's fist.

The fighter is NICO VASQUEZ-BELL (20s, shirtless, shaved head, a tattooed rosary across his collarbone). He is staring at the floor.

At the edge of the ring, leaning on the rope, stands their rival's manager, SILAS KRAUSE (50s, camel coat, gold watch).

                    SILAS
          Imelda. Lovely venue.

                    IMELDA
          Silas. You're early.

                    SILAS
          I like to watch the boy warm up.

                    NICO
          (not looking up)
          I'm warm.

                    SILAS
          Of course you are.

Imelda finishes the tape. Snips it. Pats Nico's glove.

                    IMELDA
          Don't listen to him.

                    NICO
          I'm not.

                    SILAS
          I've brought a gift for the champion.

He places a thick envelope on the ring apron. No one touches it.

                    IMELDA
          We don't take gifts.

                    SILAS
          It's not a gift. It's an opportunity.

                    NICO
          Ma, what is he talking about?

Imelda doesn't answer. She stares at Silas. He stares back.

                    IMELDA
          Get out of my gym.

                    SILAS
          Imelda, be sensible.

                    IMELDA ^
          Get out.

Silas lifts both hands in surrender and steps off the platform. He pauses at the edge.

                    SILAS
          Think about the boy's future.

He walks off along the dark tunnel. His footsteps echo and fade. Nico finally lifts his head.

                    NICO
          How much?

                    IMELDA
          Don't.

                    NICO
          How much, Ma?

She picks up the envelope and weighs it in her palm. Then she tosses it onto the ring floor.

                    IMELDA
          Open it.

Nico climbs into the ring and tears it open. Inside: stacked bills. And a folded note. He reads it. His jaw tightens.

                    NICO
          He wants me to go down in the fourth.

                    IMELDA
          And?

                    NICO
          And nothing.

He crumples the note, drops it, and begins to shadowbox. Fast. Ugly. Violent. The bulbs swing above him. Imelda watches from the apron, arms folded.

                    IMELDA
          (quietly)
          Again.

He keeps punching. Faster. His breath comes in sobs. The shadows leap across the tile.

                    NICO
          (through his teeth)
          Forty years you've been in this gym.

                    IMELDA
          Forty-three.

                    NICO
          Why'd you let him in?

                    IMELDA
          Because I needed to see what you'd do.

He stops. He stands in the center of the ring, chest heaving. The envelope lies at his feet.

                    NICO
          And?

                    IMELDA
          And you're ready.

She tosses him a mouthguard. He catches it. A train rumbles in the distance, though no trains have run here for decades, and the entire platform trembles.

                    NICO
          (grinning, wild)
          Fourth round.

                    IMELDA
          Fourth round.

He bites down on the mouthguard. She ducks through the ropes with the stool. The bulbs go out. In the dark, a single bell rings.
